SimonSays TODO

Before 0.7:
* Mention the SimonSays web tools (https://github.com/juan-rey/simonsays-web) wherever users would look for them: simonsays-board-editor (create and edit .ssc/.ssz boards in the browser: live preview, styles, templates, ARASAAC pictograms) and simonsays-board-player (show a board on a website and speak its phrases, with sounds). Candidates: HELP.md "Importing and exporting categories", "Customizing the look" and "Feedback, support and privacy"; README "Web / WordPress" (currently mentions only the editor - add the player); the Microsoft Store descriptions (EN + ES). Link public demo pages once they exist.

Before 1.0:
* Integrate eye-tracking (Windows Eye Control at minimum) to drive phrase selection and playback.
* Add a board-style authoring UI (docs/specs/board-style.spec.md §18).
* Translate the restructured English HELP.md into the 16 docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1. This includes the new table of contents and section order (everyday use first, editing afterwards), the new sections (Default phrases, Using SimonSays in online meetings, Sounds included with SimonSays, Undoing changes, Where SimonSays keeps your files, Feedback, support and privacy), and the two older untranslated parts: "Customizing the look (board & category styles)" and the PNG/JPG icon-format note.
* Translate the updated icon-format Help note (PNG/JPG icons, HELP.md "Setting or changing a category icon") into the docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1.
* Fix Ctrl+F8 (delete all categories): the SaveCategoriesToRegistry call is commented out (src/CategoryWindow.cpp:1678), so the deletion is not saved until the next edit, and the "This action cannot be undone" warning is inaccurate either way.
* Add tooltips to the main window's quick access buttons (open a board, Settings). SSButton has no tooltip support at all, so this means a new BTN- feature (a TOOLTIPS_CLASS control owned by SSButton) plus two localized strings; today the buttons only carry a window text as their screen-reader name (settings.spec.md SET-N04).
* Revisit the quick access button hit size (MW_DEFAULT_ICON_BUTTON_SIZE, currently 20px, two stacked): small for dwell/gaze users, who are a primary audience (docs/specs/dwell.spec.md).
* Remove the dead in-app HelpWindow: src/HelpWindow.cpp/.h, the m_helpWindow member and its call sites in src/MainWindow.cpp, and the retired HELP_CONTENT_ID define in include/stdafx.h. F1 now opens the shipped HTML pages, so the window is unreachable; it is kept only so the existing code still compiles.
* Select custom output device for playback.
* Have native speakers review the European Portuguese interface strings (PORTUGUESE_LOCALIZED_UI_STRINGS in include/localized_strings.h), the Brazilian Portuguese help (docs/help/HELP_pt_BR.md), and both Portuguese default phrase sets (include/default_phrases.h).

Possible Long Term Goals:
* Sound effects library expansion and user customization options.
* Flow fill: option to use the spare room in the category window to fill it with the following categories' phrases (a continuous, gap-free grid) instead of leaving empty space below the selected category's phrases.
